## Unresolved concern
Going back to canonical `:hash` brings back the P2 cost from the last round. Each stack or register input re-hashes the whole concatenated image, so N inputs cost O(N²) hashing in total, and all earlier code stays in memory. The canonical-hash rule means this can't be fixed inside the REPL loaders alone. Two options:
- Start each input on a fresh image, which needs a separate way for later inputs to reach closures from earlier ones.
- Change the H/R contract to allow an incremental form.

Either one needs a design decision from the Architect or you.
